Warranty coverage represents significant risk transfer from consumers to manufacturers. Refurbished products with limited warranty coverage signal quality uncertainty and shift risk back to consumers. Comprehensive warranty coverage for refurbished products signals manufacturer confidence in refurbishment quality.

Warranty parity removes major psychological barrier to refurbished purchases where consumers fear being disadvantaged. Manufacturer-backed warranties create conditions where refurbished products compete fairly with new products on risk-adjusted basis. Extended warranty coverage for refurbished products compensates for older component age and accumulated cycles.